  <regions type="content">
    <region left="0" top="0" width="745" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-weight: bold;">4. Analyze the following first-order RC network using DC Sweep and Transient Analysis. Use both PULSE and PWL voltage-source excitations</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="36" width="245" height="159" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="306" top="36" width="424" height="142" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="198" width="777" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>A. DC Sweep: Set V1 as a DC source and sweep it from 0 V to 5 V. Plot V(vout) as a function of the source voltage and compare the simulated result with the resistive-divider calculation. Use .dc V1 0 5 0.1</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="252" width="95" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">V.in</e>
          <e type="operand">5</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">volt</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="135" top="252" width="89" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">R.1</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kohm</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="261" top="252" width="89" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">R.2</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kohm</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="279" width="230" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">V.out</e>
          <e type="operand">V.in</e>
          <e type="operand">R.2</e>
          <e type="operand">R.1</e>
          <e type="operand">R.2</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="bracket">(</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">3.3333</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="342" width="772" height="167" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="504" width="765" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>B. Pulse response. Replace the DC source with the PULSE definition below and run a transient simulation. Plot V(vin), V(vout), and I(C1).</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="540" width="314" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Source definition:  PULSE(0 5 1m 10u 10u 4m 8m)<br />Simulation directive:  .tran 0 25m 0 10u<br /></p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="576" width="772" height="167" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="738" width="762" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Calculate the expected time constant τ = (R1 || R2)·C1. Using the LTspice cursors, estimate the charging and discharging time constants from the waveform and compare them with the theoretical value. Also explain why the final value of Vout is not 5 V.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="774" width="73" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">C.1</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">μF</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="234" top="774" width="525" height="42" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="525" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>According to \[REGION[a56a8915650e43518bb5049541cc67f1]]\</p>
        </content>
        <regions>
          <region id="a56a8915650e43518bb5049541cc67f1" left="80" top="0" width="213" height="41" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
            <math>
              <input>
                <e type="operand">τ</e>
                <e type="function" args="1">v.c</e>
                <e type="operand">V.f</e>
                <e type="operand">V.0</e>
                <e type="operand">V.f</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
                <e type="bracket">(</e>
                <e type="operand">e</e>
                <e type="operand">1</e>
                <e type="operator" args="1">-</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
                <e type="bracket">(</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
              </input>
            </math>
          </region>
        </regions>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="801" width="201" height="63" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">τ</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand">R.1</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand">R.2</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operand">C.1</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">0.0007</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">s</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="234" top="819" width="212" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">v.0_t</e>
          <e type="operand">0.632</e>
          <e type="operand">V.out</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">2.1067</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="567" top="819" width="224" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">v.3.3_t</e>
          <e type="operand">0.368</e>
          <e type="operand">V.out</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">1.2267</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="225" top="846" width="262" height="114" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="567" top="846" width="184" height="118" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="972" width="461" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Vout value is not 5v because the Vin voltage is divided between R1 and R2.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="999" width="640" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>
            <span style="font-weight: normal;">C. PWL excitation. Replace the PULSE source with the repeating triangular waveform below and</span>
            <span />
            <br />
            <span style="font-weight: normal;">simulate for at least three periods. Plot V(vin) and V(vout) on the same graph and describe the attenuation</span>
            <span />
            <br />
            <span style="font-weight: normal;">and time delay introduced by the RC network.</span>
            <span />
            <br />
            <span />
            <span />
          </p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1080" width="458" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Source definition: PWL REPEAT FOREVER (0 0 2m 5 4m 0) ENDREPEAT<br />Suggested transient analysis: .tran 0 12m 0 10u</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1125" width="772" height="167" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1314" width="763" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The RC network attenuates and delays the output because the capacitor voltage cannot change instantaneously. The resistive divider reduces the voltage, while the capacitor requires time to charge and discharge through the resistors.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1359" width="700" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The rounded corners show the low-pass filtering effect of the RC network, which smooths rapid changes in the input.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
  </regions>
